# Xymon unified access-control list (loaded by xymond via --acl=FILE).
#
# Each rule is:   SOURCE   TRANSPORT   CAPS   [force]
#   SOURCE     a v4/v6 CIDR (a bare address is a host), "local" (loopback),
#              "cert:*" (any verified client cert) or "cert:<id>" (a named one)
#   TRANSPORT  "any", "plain" (cleartext only) or "tls" (encrypted only)
#   CAPS       any of  status,www,maint,admin  (or "all")
#   force      acknowledge an intentionally broad admin grant (see below)
#
# First match wins; if no rule matches, the request is DENIED. Order rules
# specific-before-general. A trailing "# ..." is a comment. The local backfeed
# IPC channel is always trusted regardless of the rules below. Full reference:
# docs/ipv6-tls.md.
#
# This shipped default reproduces the historical posture: the loopback host and
# the server's own IP have full administrative access, and every other sender
# may report status and run www/maint queries but NOT admin. Tighten it for your
# site -- e.g. require TLS from off-net senders, or grant admin to a named cert:
#
#     cert:ops-admin  tls   all                 # a named admin identity
#     2001:db8::/32   any   status,www,maint    # your IPv6 intranet
#     cert:*          tls   status,www          # any verified cert: reporter only
#
# To grant admin to a broad source (cert:* or a CIDR wider than /24 v4 / /120
# v6) xymond requires an explicit "force" on that rule, so "everyone is admin"
# can't happen by accident.
#
# NOTE: this is a template. The @XYMONHOSTIP_ADMIN@ marker below is replaced at
# build time (make cfgfiles) with a rule granting admin to the server's own IP
# -- the old --admin-senders=127.0.0.1,$XYMONSERVERIP behaviour -- or dropped if
# the server IP is loopback. It must precede the catch-all rules (first match
# wins).

local         any   all                 # loopback: full administrative access
@XYMONHOSTIP_ADMIN@
0.0.0.0/0     any   status,www,maint    # any IPv4 sender: report/query, no admin
::/0          any   status,www,maint    # any IPv6 sender: report/query, no admin
